//! Error: a function body must be a block or an inline string, never absent
//! Tags: parser, fn, silent-fallback

// `finish_fn_def` answered a missing body with `extern_body.unwrap_or(ExternC)`.
// Only the `extern fn` caller passes `Some`, so every other bodyless form --
// plain `fn`, `co fn`, `operator`, `inline(<backend>) fn` -- silently became an
// extern C declaration that type-checked and then failed at RUNTIME with
// "attempt to call global 'c' (a nil value)". The comment there claimed the
// non-extern callers never reached it; they did.
//
// A bare `extern fn f() -> int` (no body, no `= "..."`) is still legal and is
// covered positively in the extern suite -- this rejection is for the forms
// that are NOT foreign declarations.

//=== TEST CASE: plain_fn_without_a_body ===
fn c(x: int) -> int

fn main() {
    let _ = c(1)
}
